<BaseLayout
  title="Agricultural Machinery Batteries — DINWEYS OEM"
  description="Heavy-duty starting batteries for tractors, combines and harvesters — high-CCA diesel starting, vibration-resistant construction, and off-season storage resilience. OEM supply from Chengguang Power Tech Co., Ltd."
  jsonLd={faqJsonLd}
>
  <div class="container section">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="font-size:0.9rem;color:#55606e;margin-bottom:16px;">
      <a href="/" style="color:#1e5aa8;">Home</a> &rsaquo; Applications &rsaquo; Agricultural Machinery
    </nav>
    <h1 style="color:#0f1f3d;">Agricultural Machinery Batteries</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Tractors, combines, harvesters and sprayers run diesel engines in rough, dusty, uneven fields —
      and then sit idle for weeks or months between seasons. The battery has to deliver a hard crank
      on demand while surviving long storage spells that quietly drain it.
    </p>

    <div style="margin:20px 0;padding:16px 20px;background:#f4f7fb;border-left:4px solid #f5a623;border-radius:6px;">
      <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin:0 0 10px;font-size:1.15rem;">Direct Answer</h2>
      <p style="margin:0;">Agricultural machinery needs a high-CCA diesel starting battery that also survives long idle spells between seasons. Tractors and combines commonly run 12V on smaller units and 24V (two 12V in series) on larger machines, with 850&ndash;1100+ CCA for the diesel. The battery group follows the machine &mdash; JIS N150/N200 or DIN88/DIN100 &mdash; and the biggest preventable failure is off-season self-discharge: a charged, maintained battery survives storage, while a flat one sulphates and dies before the first start.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Key Takeaways</h2>
    <ol class="takeaways-list">
      <li><strong>Diesel starting is the core demand.</strong> High CCA (850&ndash;1100+) to crank the diesel, with the group and voltage matched to the specific machine.</li>
      <li><strong>Off-season storage is the biggest killer.</strong> A battery left discharged over winter or between harvests sulphates and loses capacity, then fails on the first hard start.</li>
      <li><strong>Vibration and dust are constant on the field.</strong> Rough ground and airborne dust demand a rugged, securely held battery — flooded thick-plate or sealed AGM.</li>
      <li><strong>Keep it charged during storage.</strong> A fully charged battery self-discharges slowly; a maintenance charger or periodic top-up prevents the seasonal failure.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Why Farm Machinery Needs a Different Battery</h2>
    <p>
      A farm machine faces two opposing stresses. In use, it works on rough, uneven ground that
      transmits constant vibration, and in dry conditions airborne dust settles on terminals and
      battery tops. Out of use, it sits for weeks or months between seasons — and a lead-acid
      battery left standing self-discharges, then sulphates if it is not recharged, permanently
      losing capacity. The first cold or heavy start of the new season is then the moment the
      weakened battery finally fails.
    </p>
    <p>
      The answer is a heavy-duty battery engineered for diesel cranking plus a storage routine.
      Thick Pb-Sb (lead-antimony) flooded plates deliver the high CCA and tolerate vibration, while
      a sealed AGM removes the electrolyte-loss and dust problems of a vented unit and resists the
      deeper cycling that comes with repeated cold starts and auxiliary loads. DINWEYS supplies both
      — flooded JIS N150/N200 and DIN88/DIN100 for standard budgets, and AGM where the duty justifies
      a maintenance-free option.
    </p>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Duty Cycle &amp; Environment</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Factor</th><th>Agricultural duty</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Duty cycle</td><td>Seasonal and intermittent: intense use during planting and harvest, then long idle periods between seasons that drain a standing battery.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Starting demand</td><td>850&ndash;1100+ CCA (SAE J537) for diesel engines; 12V on smaller tractors, 24V (2&times; 12V series) on larger machines.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Environment</td><td>Vibration on rough, uneven fields; airborne dust; temperature swings including cold-morning starts; occasional slope operation.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Battery requirements</td><td>High-CCA diesel starting, thick-plate flooded or sealed AGM construction, and a storage/charging routine for the off-season.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Recommended characteristics</td><td>Choose by cranking demand and storage pattern &mdash; AGM resists vibration and self-discharges slower than flooded, but flooded remains the lower-cost standard for simple starting duty.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Recommended Specifications</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Specification</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>System voltage</td><td>12V for smaller tractors; 24V (two 12V batteries in series) for larger tractors, combines and harvesters</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cold Cranking Amps</td><td>850–1100+ CCA (SAE J537) for diesel engines</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Group size</td><td>JIS N150/N200 (Japanese/Korean machines) or DIN88/DIN100 (European machines)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Construction</td><td>Thick-plate flooded (Pb-Sb) or sealed AGM</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Storage behaviour</td><td>AGM self-discharges more slowly than flooded and resists sulphation better when standing; both benefit from a maintenance charge during storage</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Test schedule</td><td>Load-test before each season; inspect hold-downs and terminals every service</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="data-note">
      Specifications are representative ranges. Exact CCA, capacity and dimensions vary by machine —
      contact us for a datasheet matched to your equipment.
    </p>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Product Lines for Agricultural Duty</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:16px;">
